  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Environmental Governance, Inclusion &amp; Transparency in Mining Sector IDF Grant Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the proposed IDF grant is to support the implementation capacity of the Government of Armenia and key stakeholders to improve environmental governance, inclusion and transparency in the use of country&apos;s mineral resources. The aim of the assistance would be to build institutional capacity of key agencies (e.g., Minisitry of Energy and Natural Resources and Ministry of Environment) to complete the development of and implement mining and environment regulatory framework. This will be in line with good international practice and norms, and the Government of Armenia&apos;s sustainability goals, by  engaging the private sector, society and communities; ensuring that mining takes place in a socially and environmentally responsible manner, including the revenues from the sector benefit the population as a whole, and mining communities in particular. The GOA&apos;s requested the IDF assistance to support its overall objective to balance industrial growth and sustainable development following the Bank&apos;s policy development support provided in 2011-2012.  TF013658 The development objective of the proposed project is to improve the capacity of key Government agencies to address institutional and implementation gaps concerning environmental and social regulations in the mining sector.</narrative>
  </description>
